Yes—that is the physically correct concern.

A hard landing is not merely “camera moves down to slow the fall.” If the player cannot absorb the impact, the body stops while the head keeps moving briefly, so the head can strike the ground.

The system therefore needs:

- a bounded head/body compression spring for ordinary landings;
- a sharp residual head-impact response when the landing delta-v exceeds what the body can absorb;
- no camera clipping through the floor;
- impact severity tied to the same resolved delta-v used for movement and damage.

The current code models capsule landing plus a visual dip, but it does not yet model a distinct head-impact consequence.

